    <forecast>
        <area aac="SA_FA001" description="South Australia" type="region">
            <forecast-period start-time-local="2026-11-19T11:38:10+10:30" end-time-local="2026-11-19T11:38:10+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-11-19T01:08:10Z" end-time-utc="2026-11-19T01:08:10Z">
                <text type="warning_summary_footer">For latest warnings go to www.bom.gov.au, subscribe to RSS feeds, call 1300 659 210* or listen for warnings on relevant TV and radio broadcasts.</text>
                <text type="synoptic_situation">A low pressure system and associated trough over Western Australia move across the state during Thursday, clearing to the east early Friday. A high pressure system will then move across southern SA from Friday, before a trough and cold front move across the west late Saturday and across the rest of SA on Sunday.</text>
                <text type="product_footer">* Calls to 1300 numbers cost around 27.5c incl. GST, higher from mobiles or public phones.</text>
            </forecast-period>
        </area>
        <area aac="SA_PW009" description="Flinders" type="public-district" parent-aac="SA_FA001">
            <forecast-period index="0" start-time-local="2026-11-19T00:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-11-20T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-11-18T13:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-11-19T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Partly cloudy. High chance of showers, most likely in the late afternoon and evening. A thunderstorm likely, possibly severe with damaging winds, large hail and heavy rain which may lead to flash flooding. Winds north to northeasterly 25 to 35 km/h tending north to northwesterly in the early afternoon then turning northeasterly 15 to 25 km/h during the afternoon and evening. Daytime maximum temperatures in the low to mid 30s.</text>
                <text type="fire_danger">High</text>
                <text type="uv_alert">Sun protection 9:00am to 5:00pm, UV Index predicted to reach 11 [Extreme]</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="1" start-time-local="2026-11-20T00:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-11-21T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-11-19T13:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-11-20T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Slight chance of a shower in the late morning and early afternoon. The chance of a thunderstorm in the morning and early afternoon. Sunny afternoon. Winds northwest to northeasterly 15 to 20 km/h tending westerly 25 to 35 km/h in the morning then turning south to southwesterly 20 to 30 km/h during the day. Overnight temperatures falling to between 15 and 19 with daytime temperatures reaching the low to mid 30s.</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="2" start-time-local="2026-11-21T00:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-11-22T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-11-20T13:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-11-21T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Mostly sunny. The chance of morning fog south of Hawker. Winds southeast to southwesterly 15 to 25 km/h becoming light during the morning then becoming west to northwesterly 15 to 25 km/h during the day. Overnight temperatures falling to between 11 and 17 with daytime temperatures reaching the low to mid 30s.</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="3" start-time-local="2026-11-22T00:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-11-23T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-11-21T13:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-11-22T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Partly cloudy. Slight chance of a shower. The chance of a thunderstorm in the morning. Winds northwest to northeasterly 30 to 45 km/h tending west to northwesterly during the day then tending west to southwesterly 25 to 40 km/h during the afternoon. Overnight temperatures falling to 21 to 26 with daytime temperatures reaching 33 to 39.</text>
            </forecast-period>
        </area>
